        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "16eeff50-2adc-5462-963d-c3b0ef84cc0c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Crawford Ashley, Virgil Hill, Yawe Davis, Graciano Rocchigiani, Michael Nunn, Sebastiaan Rothmann\n- Organizations: British Boxing Board of Control, European Boxing Union, World Boxing Association, World Boxing Union\n- Places: Leeds\n- Roles: professional boxer, amateur boxer\n- Topics: boxing titles, weight classes, 1984 Summer Olympics\n\nFacts:\n- Virgil Hill won a silver medal in the middleweight division at the 1984 Summer Olympics as an amateur.\n- Crawford Ashley was born Gary Crawford on 20 May 1964 in Leeds.\n- Crawford Ashley was an English professional boxer who fought during the 1980s, 1990s, and 2000s.\n- Crawford Ashley competed at weights ranging from 163 pounds in super middleweight to 211 pounds in heavyweight.\n- Crawford Ashley won the British Boxing Board of Control Central Area light heavyweight title and the British Boxing Board of Control British light heavyweight title.\n- Crawford Ashley won the European Boxing Union light heavyweight title twice and the Commonwealth light heavyweight title twice.\n- Crawford Ashley drew with Yawe Davis for the vacant European Boxing Union light heavyweight title.\n- Crawford Ashley challenged Graciano Rocchigiani for the European Boxing Union light heavyweight title.\n- Crawford Ashley challenged Michael Nunn for the World Boxing Association World super middleweight title.\n- Crawford Ashley challenged Virgil Hill for the World Boxing Association World light heavyweight title.\n- Crawford Ashley challenged Sebastiaan Rothmann for the World Boxing Union cruiserweight title.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ce616516-4b0b-5d87-bdca-1cf4203db55f",
        "text": "Page: Crawford Ashley. Sentence: Crawford \"Chilling\" Ashley (born Gary Crawford, 20 May 1964 in Leeds is an English professional super middle/light heavy/cruiser/heavyweight boxer of the 1980s, '90s and 2000s, who won the British Boxing Board of Control (BBBofC) Central Area light heavyweight title, BBBofC British light heavyweight title, European Boxing Union (EBU) light heavyweight title (twice), and Commonwealth light heavyweight title (twice), drew with Yawe Davis for the vacant European Boxing Union (EBU) light heavyweight title, and was a challenger for the European Boxing Union (EBU) light heavyweight title against Graciano Rocchigiani, World Boxing Association (WBA) World super middleweight title against Michael Nunn, World Boxing Association (WBA) World light heavyweight title against Virgil Hill, and World Boxing Union (WBU) cruiserweight title against Sebastiaan Rothmann, his professional fighting weight varied from 163 lb , i.e. super middleweight to 211 lb , i.e. heavyweight.\nPage: Virgil Hill. Sentence: As an amateur, Hill won a silver medal in the middleweight division at the 1984 Summer Olympics.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
